Final file:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Runtime.InteropServices;

public static class NativeCompression
{
    [DllImport("compresslib", EntryPoint = "compress_buffer",
        CallingConvention = CallingConvention.Cdecl, ExactSpelling = true)]
    public static extern int CompressBuffer(
        [In] byte[] input,
        UIntPtr inputLen,
        [Out] byte[] output,
        UIntPtr outputLen,
        out UIntPtr bytesWritten);
}
```

The `EntryPoint` maps the C# method name `CompressBuffer` to the native export `compress_buffer`. On x86 .NET Framework, `UIntPtr` is 4 bytes — matching `size_t` for a 32-bit target.
